  "id": "DrugBank_DB00958 - MONDO_3795",
  "verbalization": "Carboplatin, a platinum-based chemotherapy agent, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Carboplatin is associated with Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma and Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor of Ovary, both of which are linked to Tretamine. Tretamine, in turn, is indicated to cause Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma. This chain of indications implies a potential mechanism by which Carboplatin may influence the development of Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma, possibly through the activation of pathways that are regulated by Tretamine. The recurring association with Tretamine suggests a possible role in the oncogenic process, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential link between Carboplatin and Ovarian Small Cell Carcinoma through the indirect pathway involving Tretamine, highlighting the importance of Tretamine in the oncogenic cascade.",
